  "notes": "Compact 2-storey corner villa in two tones: protruding cream entry block (#ebe3ce) with a horizontal-slat siding strip along its top (#e5dbbf), a stone-brick accent patch at its lower-left (#d9cfb4) and a light stone-block base course (#cbc3ad); recessed wooden entrance door (#a46e45) at the inside corner; beige main block (#cbba9c) carrying the barred window stack. Red clay-tile GABLE roof #c76d5b (ridge runs across the plan; gable end over the right wall, which is clad in lighter horizontal siding #f1e6c9 - band schema has no facade key so noted here). All windows have grey security-bar grilles #a0a09a in front of the glass (no bars field yet). There is an extra mid-level stairwell window between floors on the front at x~0.45 (schema is per-floor, noted for factory). FRONTAGE: NO brick wall - a wood horizontal-slat fence (#b07246 slats, grey steel posts #5e5c68, h~1.4 per spec) with a steel-framed slat pedestrian gate; right of the gate the fence sits on a white stone-block wall base (#d0bca5) - slat fence type pending in factory. Inside the fence an orange brick-paved forecourt (#dc8c68). Tall beige-brick neighbour compound wall (#d8c4a7) closes the left edge of the frame. Sidewalk is tan paving brick to the kerb, no grass verge; road not visible in ref (asphalt hex copied from style anchor). Vegetation for prop factory: two round low-poly trees right (#80b03c canopy, dark #30592a), a palm-like shrub behind the fence, a small globe tree at the entrance; grass field horizon #7eac42. White gutter + downpipe on the entry block. Sampled from 12x9 scene grid + 24x18 iso grid 2026-07-03."
